"""Net part 4a: the transport's UDP socket (net/net_socket.cpp lines 18-end) against the original's (net/sock_diff.cpp,
suite net.sock; run with HD2_SOCK_QUICK=1 on build_sock.bat, every file built with -include sock_fakes.h, linked with
-Wl,--image-base=0x20000000 -lws2_32).

277 mutants, 19 not building; 249 of the 258 building killed. The 9 left, all equivalent or unobservable:
- LoadDword copying 5 bytes into its 4-byte local (25 num: the byte past it is never read);
- the fragments' order comparing messages with <= (38 cmp: reached only when they differ);
- an 801-byte fragment buffer (52 num);
- the destructor's DeleteCriticalSection (59 del);
- Open's test for an open socket against -2 (66 num: Close returns at once on a closed one);
- the bound address's zeroing (73 del: the sockaddr is zeroed whole already);
- a small message's pool buffer of size + 4 or size - 3 (126 num, arith: under 1000 bytes either way, the same pool
  buffer);
- FindComplete's index test with > (218 cmp: the loop has bounded the index already)."""
